OL,3,GNEWSAFootball families call for action
OL,4,Aon headers
OL,5,
OL,6,FCampaigners have called on the
OL,7,Fgovernment to take urgent action to
OL,8,Fmake clear the health risks associated
OL,9,Fwith heading footballs.
OL,11,FCharity Head Safe Football, set up by
OL,12,FDr Judith Gates after the death of her
OL,13,Fhusband, former Middlesbrough player
OL,14,FBill, has launched a national petition
OL,15,Fto declare heading the ball a public
OL,16,Fhealth issue.
OL,18,FResearchers have found footballers are
OL,19,Fthree and a half times more likely to
OL,20,Fdie from a neurodegenerative disease
OL,21,Fthan the general population.
OL,23,APub: 13-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
